    "body": "**TLDR:** W&B drops every validation metric logged at a step that training already logged. With the default `log_freq=10` and validator `freq=10`, that is every core validation; in RL, it is the post-training pass and, with the next PR, every periodic pass. `WandBLogger` now accumulates each step's row and pushes it with an explicit `commit()`.\n\n**Problem**\n1. `WandBLogger.log` calls `wandb.log(metrics, step=N, commit=True)`, so each step shows up in W&B as soon as it is logged.\n2. Once row N is committed, W&B drops every later log to step N.\n3. Validation logs after training at the same step, so `validation_metrics/*` never lands.\n4. RL's post-training validation logs at the last train step (`Controller.run`), so the same rule drops it.\n\n**Solution**\n1. `WandBLogger.log` accumulates into the step's row (W&B's default when `step` is passed).\n2. A new `commit()` on the loggers pushes the open row. The trainer calls it after validation.\n3. The RL controller calls it at the top of each step and after post-training validation, so that pass joins the last row.\n4. Each step still shows up in W&B as soon as its last log lands.\n\n**Results**\n\nCommitted rows read back from the offline `.wandb` file (W&B 0.28.1).\n\n1-GPU llama3 debugmodel, `log_freq=5`, validator `freq=5`, measured on an earlier main (losses differ slightly: no fixed seed):\n```\nmain:\n{'_step': 1,  'loss_metrics/global_avg_loss': 8.08}\n{'_step': 5,  'loss_metrics/global_avg_loss': 5.24}\n{'_step': 10, 'loss_metrics/global_avg_loss': 4.11}\n\nthis PR:\n{'_step': 1,  'loss_metrics/global_avg_loss': 8.08, 'validation_metrics/loss': 7.77}\n{'_step': 5,  'loss_metrics/global_avg_loss': 5.22, 'validation_metrics/loss': 4.69}\n{'_step': 10, 'loss_metrics/global_avg_loss': 3.99, 'validation_metrics/loss': 4.00}\n```\n\nThe RL controller's log/commit order with overlapped validation (next PR), replayed through the real `WandBLogger`, 6 steps:\n```\nmain:     6 rows, train/loss only\nthis PR:  step 1  train/loss, validation/pass_0\n          step 3  train/loss, validation/pass_2\n          step 6  train/loss, validation/pass_4, validation/final\n```\n\nYou may ask: why not just drop `commit=True`? Then row N is pushed only when the next logged step arrives, so every row shows up late (up to `log_freq` steps, or one RL step).\nYou may ask: why not a custom x-axis, `define_metric(\"*\", step_metric=\"step\")`? `_step` would stop matching the training step, which breaks panels of older runs and `WANDB_RESUME_FROM`/`WANDB_FORK_FROM=<run>?_step=N`.\n\nNOTE: `experiments/torchft/trainer.py` has its own loop and doesn't call `commit()`. Its rows are pushed when the next step logs: correct, one logged step late.\n\n**Test plan**\n```\npytest tests/unit_tests/cpu/observability/ tests/unit_tests/cpu/test_torchft_trainer.py tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu/test_metrics.py   # 226 passed\npytest tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu   # 511 passed, 8 skipped, same as main\n```\nNew: `test_wandb_commit_keeps_validation_in_the_training_row`. The next PR's `test_overlapped_validation_runs_beside_training` checks the RL commit order. The RL replay script is not checked in.\n",
